---
description: Extract every new UI or gameplay piece into a reusable component
alwaysApply: true
---

# Reusable components

Every new UI or gameplay piece is its own reusable component. Do not leave one-off markup or behavior inline in a page, scene, or parent.

- One component per file, in its own folder grouped by scope (`src/components/PokemonCard/`).
- Export a props type above the component. Pass variation in through props (data, callbacks, visual variants). Do not hardcode a single caller, Pokémon, or screen.
- Co-locate CSS in that folder. Style the component from its own props. Do not write selectors that style child components; pass props into the child and let it style itself.
- Keep the component under 120 lines. Split a larger piece into smaller reusable components.
- A component built for one screen must still work on another screen with different props.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — one-off markup and a hardcoded Pokémon inside the page
export function BattleScreen() {
  return <div className="card">Charmander · Fire</div>
}

// ✅ GOOD — src/components/PokemonCard/PokemonCard.tsx
export type PokemonCardProps = {
  pokemon: Pokemon
  selected?: boolean
  onSelect?: (id: PokemonId) => void
}

export function PokemonCard({ pokemon, selected = false, onSelect }: PokemonCardProps) {
  return (
    <button type="button" data-selected={selected} onClick={() => onSelect?.(pokemon.id)}>
      {pokemon.name}
    </button>
  )
}
```
